=== Nested Scoping Sample ===
--- 1. Class in class ---
  Outer.Inner (class in class)
--- 2. Struct in class ---
  Outer.NestedPoint(x, y) struct nested in class
--- 3. Abstract type in class ---
  Outer.IAction abstract type nested in class
--- 4. Abstract type in class ---
  Outer.Describable abstract type nested in class
--- 5. Enum in class ---
  Outer.Status: Active=Active, Inactive=Inactive, Pending=Pending
--- 6. Class in struct ---
  ContainerStruct.Item declared (see NestedInStruct.mist, readonly emitter limitation)
--- 7. Class in abstract type ---
  IFactory.DefaultProduct declared (see NestedInAbstract.mist)
--- 8. Class in abstract type ---
  Serializable.Config declared (see NestedInAbstract.mist)
--- 9. Deeply nested types (4 levels) ---
  Level1.Level2.Level3.Level4 (4 levels deep)
--- 10. Generic parent type parameter access ---
  Box<T>.Wrapper nested in generic parent (exercised internally via DemoWrapper)
--- 11. Multiple sibling nested types ---
  Entry=Registry.Entry, Metadata=Registry.Metadata, Category.System=System, Category.User=User, Category.Plugin=Plugin
--- 12. Nested block namespaces ---
  Networking.Protocol.TcpHandler (nested block namespace)
--- 13. Repeated block namespaces ---
  StringHelper.Upper("test") = test
  MathHelper.Add(3, 4) = 7
--- 14. File-scoped namespace with nested types ---
  NestedScoping.Outer contains Inner, NestedPoint, IAction, Describable, Status
  Verified via Outer.DemoClassInClass(): Outer.Inner (class in class)
--- 15. Qualified name references from within parent ---
  Inner.Hello() called from Outer.DemoClassInClass()
  Status.Active called from Outer.DemoEnumInClass()
  Entry.Kind(), Metadata.Kind(), Category.System called from Registry.DemoSiblings()
  Level4.Depth() called from Level3.UseLevel4()
  All verified: Outer.Inner (class in class)
--- 16. Nested types in type positions ---
  class: Widget x5, Gadget x3
  struct: Bolt:100
=== Nested Scoping Done ===
